Not sing. Boop's own stand-in for the two packages of github.com/sagernet/sing
(GPL-3.0-or-later) that the parts of Xray-core (MPL-2.0) linked into Boop.exe
import, so that no GPL code ends up in the exe. desktop/go.mod points
github.com/sagernet/sing here with a replace directive.

  common/control  the type of a socket hook, control.Func (what
                  transport/internet keeps its dialer and listener hooks in)
  common/uot      UDP-over-TCP's magic addresses and NewServerConn, used by
                  app/proxyman/outbound for a destination named
                  "sp.v2.udp-over-tcp.arpa": Boop never dials a name (only IP
                  addresses), and here such a connection fails instead of
                  starting a UoT server.

Written for Boop from the names Xray-core uses; no code from sing. If a new
Xray-core imports more of sing, the build fails here, and the new import has to
be looked at the same way (go list -deps ./... | grep sagernet).
